00:33:53.410 --> 00:33:57.360
And I'll start with the
reduction on human error

00:33:57.360 --> 00:34:00.850
by automating the
sharing permissions.

00:34:00.850 --> 00:34:05.980
AODocs has a workflow engine,
very powerful, very agile.

00:34:05.980 --> 00:34:10.179
And you can set up
the right processes,

00:34:10.179 --> 00:34:11.380
your business processes.

00:34:11.380 --> 00:34:14.230
You can digitalize them
through the AODocs workflow.

00:34:14.230 --> 00:34:19.360
And you can set the workflows,
such as for each step

00:34:19.360 --> 00:34:22.420
of the workflow, the
right permissions

00:34:22.420 --> 00:34:25.429
apply automatically
on the documents.

00:34:25.429 --> 00:34:27.639
So instead of having
to decide manually,

00:34:27.639 --> 00:34:30.010
who am I going to share
this document with,

00:34:30.010 --> 00:34:32.230
you just create the
document directly in AODocs,

00:34:32.230 --> 00:34:35.080
click on the Workflow
button, send for validation,

00:34:35.080 --> 00:34:37.310
and the document will
be shared automatically

00:34:37.310 --> 00:34:41.880
with the right people who
need to validate the document.

00:34:41.880 --> 00:34:44.280
Also, you can use the
check-in/check-out to make sure

00:34:44.280 --> 00:34:46.830
there is no concurring
edition on the documents.

00:34:46.830 --> 00:34:49.330
So when you work on a
very important procedure,

00:34:49.330 --> 00:34:51.719
for instance, and
you need to edit it,

00:34:51.719 --> 00:34:53.230
you can check-out the documents.

00:34:53.230 --> 00:34:56.489
So it's like if you took away
a document from the office

00:34:56.489 --> 00:35:00.660
to your home, let's say, to
work on it, and you are sure--

00:35:00.660 --> 00:35:02.170
you're guaranteed by AODocs--

00:35:02.170 --> 00:35:03.900
that while you work
on this document,

00:35:03.900 --> 00:35:05.490
no one else is working on it--

00:35:05.490 --> 00:35:09.590
or at least they're not editing
it, they're just viewing it.

00:35:09.590 --> 00:35:12.980
So with the workflow, the
advanced security managements

00:35:12.980 --> 00:35:16.520
that we offer, and features
like check-in/check-out,

00:35:16.520 --> 00:35:21.540
we drastically reduce the
human error of your documents.

00:35:24.300 --> 00:35:27.480
I'll take an example of
the publication workflow.

00:35:27.480 --> 00:35:29.720
Typically, when
you need to publish

00:35:29.720 --> 00:35:33.990
a policy inside
your company, you

00:35:33.990 --> 00:35:37.770
start to create
an initial draft.

00:35:37.770 --> 00:35:39.900
So you don't need
the whole company

00:35:39.900 --> 00:35:43.650
to access the draft, just you
and maybe a few colleagues.

00:35:43.650 --> 00:35:45.830
Then you send it for approval.

00:35:45.830 --> 00:35:47.670
Here, the permissions
need to change,

00:35:47.670 --> 00:35:49.440
because you might
need to send it

00:35:49.440 --> 00:35:51.510
to the legal or the
compliance department,

00:35:51.510 --> 00:35:54.210
so that they make sure
the document is OK.

00:35:54.210 --> 00:35:55.710
Then the document is published.

00:35:55.710 --> 00:36:00.356
So it might going to be
published on your intranet.

00:36:00.356 --> 00:36:01.980
And so in this case,
you want everybody

00:36:01.980 --> 00:36:03.146
in the company to access it.

00:36:03.146 --> 00:36:05.190
So AODocs will automatically
share the document

00:36:05.190 --> 00:36:07.500
with the whole company.

00:36:07.500 --> 00:36:12.900
Then after a certain period of
time, you have two choices--

00:36:12.900 --> 00:36:16.510
either the procedure or the
policy needs to be updated.

00:36:16.510 --> 00:36:19.860
So the version one of the
policy will stay updated.

00:36:19.860 --> 00:36:23.970
You will create a draft of
a version two, work on it,

00:36:23.970 --> 00:36:27.240
process the version two
through the same workflow.

00:36:27.240 --> 00:36:29.790
And once the version
two is validated,

00:36:29.790 --> 00:36:34.260
it will be published as well
and replace the version one.

00:36:34.260 --> 00:36:39.120
After some time, if it's the
way you configured the workflow,

00:36:39.120 --> 00:36:41.880
the document can be
automatically archived,

00:36:41.880 --> 00:36:44.010
which is going to be the
case for the version one.

00:36:44.010 --> 00:36:47.590
And so it's unshared
from the whole company

00:36:47.590 --> 00:36:52.558
and shared to just a
restricted number of people.

00:36:52.558 --> 00:36:55.970
So to sum it up, the
right permissions

00:36:55.970 --> 00:36:59.270
are automatically applied at
each step of the workflow.

